323-Starter-1-Q1,mcq,Which number is an integer?,Maths,6,Integers & Operations,Number Theory,Students can define integers and represent them on a number line,Knowing,easy,1,"A 3-question Grade 6 MCQ bank on defining integers and locating them on a number line, with varied beginner-friendly difficulty and no reuse of recent standout values.","{""options"":[{""text"":""7"",""correct"":true},{""text"":""2.4"",""correct"":false},{""text"":""1/2"",""correct"":false},{""text"":""0.75"",""correct"":false}],""explanation"":""An integer is a whole number, its opposite, or 0. The number 7 is an integer."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learning_objective"":""Students can define integers and represent them on a number line"",""focus"":""Identify an integer from a list of numbers""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""323-Starter-1-Q1"",""topicId"":""323"",""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learningObjective"":""Students can define integers and represent them on a number line"",""levelTag"":""Beginner"",""topicFamily"":""Number Theory"",""grade"":6,""subject"":""Maths"",""questionCount"":1,""testType"":""Starter"",""proficiencyLevel"":""Basic"",""questionMedium"":""MCQ"",""recentQuestions"":[""Point P is 3 units to the right of 0 on a number line. Which integer is at point P?"",""True or False: The number -9 is an integer and would be placed to the left of 0 on a number line."",""A number with no fractional or decimal part, such as -9, 0, or 8, is called an ___"",""On a number line, the integer 2 is ___ of 0."",""Match each number to its correct description."",""Drag each number to the correct box to show whether it is an integer or not an integer."",""Explain what an integer is. Then write these numbers in the order they appear from left to right on a number line: -5, 0, 2, 8."",""Which of the temperatures -5°C, 0°C, and 8°C are integers? Then write them in the order they would appear from left to right on a number line.""],""recentStandoutValues"":[""2.8"",""-9"",""3/5"",""1.1"",""6"",""-5"",""8"",""-10"",""3"",""-3"",""9"",""1.5"",""4"",""1.8"",""3/4"",""5""],""avoidNumberReuse"":true,""calibrationExamples"":[{""difficultyBand"":""Basic"",""question"":""Which of the following is a negative integer?\nA) 0   B) –5   C) 3.5   D) ½"",""answer"":""B) –5"",""markingNote"":""Accept only B. If student selects 0, note they may be confusing 'negative' with 'non-positive'.""},{""difficultyBand"":""Pro"",""question"":""Plot these integers on the number line: –4, 0, 3, –1, 2.\nLabel each point clearly."",""answer"":""All 5 points plotted in correct positions relative to 0."",""markingNote"":""Deduct for incorrect spacing only if –4 is placed to the right of –1. Accept any scale as long as order is correct.""}],""questionType"":""mcq""},""batchRequest"":{""topicId"":""323"",""learningObjective"":""Students can define integers and represent them on a number line"",""testType"":""Starter"",""questionMedium"":""MCQ"",""queueIds"":[""323-Starter-1-Q1"",""323-Starter-1-Q2"",""323-Starter-1-Q8""]},""spec"":{""summary"":""A 3-question Grade 6 MCQ bank on defining integers and locating them on a number line, with varied beginner-friendly difficulty and no reuse of recent standout values.""},""deterministicValidation"":{""isValid"":true,""issues"":[]}}"
323-Starter-1-Q2,mcq,"On a number line, where is -7 located?",Maths,6,Integers & Operations,Number Theory,Students can define integers and represent them on a number line,Understanding,easy,2,"A 3-question Grade 6 MCQ bank on defining integers and locating them on a number line, with varied beginner-friendly difficulty and no reuse of recent standout values.","{""options"":[{""text"":""7 units to the right of 0"",""correct"":false},{""text"":""7 units to the left of 0"",""correct"":true},{""text"":""At the same point as 0"",""correct"":false},{""text"":""Between 0 and 1"",""correct"":false}],""explanation"":""Negative integers are placed to the left of 0 on a number line. So -7 is 7 units left of 0."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learning_objective"":""Students can define integers and represent them on a number line"",""focus"":""Locate a negative integer on a number line""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""323-Starter-1-Q2"",""topicId"":""323"",""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learningObjective"":""Students can define integers and represent them on a number line"",""levelTag"":""Beginner"",""topicFamily"":""Number Theory"",""grade"":6,""subject"":""Maths"",""questionCount"":1,""testType"":""Starter"",""proficiencyLevel"":""Basic"",""questionMedium"":""MCQ"",""recentQuestions"":[""Point P is 3 units to the right of 0 on a number line. Which integer is at point P?"",""True or False: The number -9 is an integer and would be placed to the left of 0 on a number line."",""A number with no fractional or decimal part, such as -9, 0, or 8, is called an ___"",""On a number line, the integer 2 is ___ of 0."",""Match each number to its correct description."",""Drag each number to the correct box to show whether it is an integer or not an integer."",""Explain what an integer is. Then write these numbers in the order they appear