323-Starter-1-Q10,word_problem,Which of these floor numbers are integers? Then write them in the order they would appear from left to right on a number line.,Maths,6,Integers & Operations,Number Theory,Students can define integers and represent them on a number line,Understanding,easy,1,"Generated 1 Grade 6 beginner word problem on defining integers and representing them on a number line, using a fresh scenario and avoiding recent standout values.","{""scenario"":""At a seaside elevator display, basement floors are shown with negative numbers, ground level is 0, and floors above ground are shown with positive numbers. The display shows Basement 2, Ground, Floor 1, and Floor 7."",""solutionSteps"":[""Integers are whole numbers, their opposites, and 0. They do not include fractions or decimals."",""The floor numbers shown are -2, 0, 1, and 7."",""All of these numbers are integers."",""On a number line, numbers increase from left to right."",""So the order from left to right is -2, 0, 1, 7.""],""finalAnswer"":""All the floor numbers are integers: -2, 0, 1, and 7. From left to right on the number line: -2, 0, 1, 7."",""hints"":[""Think about whether any of the numbers have decimals or fractions."",""Numbers to the left of 0 are negative, and numbers to the right of 0 are positive."",""List the numbers from smallest to greatest.""],""requiresCalculation"":false,""scoringGuidance"":""Award full marks for identifying that all given numbers are integers and for ordering them correctly as -2, 0, 1, 7 from left to right on a number line. Give partial credit if the student correctly identifies the integers but makes one ordering mistake, or if the order is correct but the explanation of integers is incomplete."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learning_objective"":""Students can define integers and represent them on a number line"",""focus"":null}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request""