323-Starter-2-Q1,mcq,Which integer is the greatest?,Maths,6,Integers & Operations,Number Theory,Students can compare and order positive and negative integers,Knowing,easy,1,"3 classroom-ready Grade 6 Maths MCQs on comparing and ordering positive and negative integers, with a beginner-friendly difficulty mix and varied numbers.","{""options"":[{""text"":""-6"",""correct"":false},{""text"":""0"",""correct"":false},{""text"":""12"",""correct"":true},{""text"":""-4"",""correct"":false}],""explanation"":""Positive integers are greater than 0 and any negative integer. Among these, 12 is the greatest."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learning_objective"":""Students can compare and order positive and negative integers"",""focus"":""compare integers""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""323-Starter-2-Q1"",""topicId"":""323"",""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learningObjective"":""Students can compare and order positive and negative integers"",""levelTag"":""Beginner"",""topicFamily"":""Number Theory"",""grade"":6,""subject"":""Maths"",""questionCount"":1,""testType"":""Starter"",""proficiencyLevel"":""Basic"",""questionMedium"":""MCQ"",""recentQuestions"":[""A mountain cabin is at 9°C, a freezer is at -14°C, a classroom is at 3°C, and a basement is at -1°C. Which place has the second highest temperature?"",""-10 is greater than 2."",""Among the integers -10, 2, and 8, the smallest number is ___."",""When the integers 9, -11, 0, and 1 are arranged from greatest to least, the first number is ___."",""Match each set of integers to its correct order from least to greatest."",""Drag each integer into the correct box to order the numbers from least to greatest."",""Write these integers in order from least to greatest: -11, 2, 8, -10, 0."",""Order the checkpoint elevations from least to greatest. Then name the checkpoint at the lowest e