323-Starter-2-Q3,true_false,"True or False: In the order from least to greatest, -12 comes before -4.",Maths,6,Integers & Operations,Number Theory,Students can compare and order positive and negative integers,Understanding,easy,1,Generated 1 true/false diagnostic item on comparing and ordering positive and negative integers for Grade 6 Maths.,"{""correctAnswer"":true,""explanation"":""This statement is true because -12 is less than -4. On a number line, numbers farther to the left are smaller, and -12 is to the left of -4."",""misconceptionNote"":""Students may think -4 is smaller because 4 is less than 12, forgetting that among negative numbers, the number with the greater absolute value is actually less."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learning_objective"":""Students can compare and order positive and negative integers"",""focus"":""compare negative integers""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""323-Starter-2-Q3"",""topicId"":""323"",""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learningObjective"":""Students can compare and order positive and negative integers"",""levelTag"":""Beginner"",""topicFamily"":""Number Theory"",""grade"":6,""subject"":""Maths"",""questionCount"":1,""testType"":""Starter"",""proficiencyLevel"":""Basic"",""questionMedium"":""T/F"",""recentQuestions"":[""A mountain cabin is at 9°C, a freezer is at -14°C, a classroom is at 3°C, and a basement is at -1°C. Which place has the second highest temperature?"",""-10 is greater than 2."",""Among the integers -10, 2, and 8, the smallest number is ___."",""When the integers 9, -11, 0, and 1 are arranged from greatest to least, the first number is ___."",""Match each set of integers to its correct order from least to greatest."",""Drag each integer into the correct box to order the numbers from least to greatest."",""Write these integers in order from least to greate