323-Starter-4-Q10,word_problem,"What is the drone’s height change after the full sequence, and is the result positive or negative?",Maths,6,Integers & Operations,Number Theory,Students can multiply and divide integers and determine the sign of the result,Applying,easy,2,Generated 1 Grade 6 word problem on multiplying and dividing integers and determining the sign of the result.,"{""scenario"":""A mountain rescue drone starts at a height represented as 0 metres. During a training sequence, it drops 18 metres each minute for 2 minutes, then rises by sharing that total change equally over 3 minutes. The final height change is compared to the starting point."",""solutionSteps"":[""First find the total drop: (-18) × 2 = -36."",""Then divide that total change equally over 3 minutes: (-36) ÷ 3 = -12."",""So the drone’s final height change is -12 metres."",""Because the result is less than 0, the sign is negative.""],""finalAnswer"":""-12 metres, negative."",""hints"":[""A drop is represented by a negative integer."",""Multiply first to find the total change over 2 minutes."",""Then divide by 3 and check whether the answer is above or below 0.""],""requiresCalculation"":true,""scoringGuidance"":""Award full marks for calculating -12 metres and stating that the result is negative. Give partial credit if the student correctly multiplies to get -36 or correctly identifies that a negative divided by a positive is negative, but makes an arithmetic error afterward."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learning_objective"":""Students can multiply and divide integers and determine the sign of the result"",""focus"":null}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""323-Starter-4-Q10"",""topicId"":""323"",""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learningObjective"":""Students can multiply and divide integers and determine the sign of the result"",""levelTag"