323-Starter-5-Q10,word_problem,What is Meena’s new bank balance? Write an integer equation and find the answer.,Maths,6,Integers & Operations,Number Theory,Students can apply integer operations to real-world contexts such as temperature and debt,Applying,easy,2,"Generated 1 beginner Grade 6 word problem on applying integer operations in a real-world context of debt, aligned to the given learning objective and avoiding recent scenario/value repetition.","{""scenario"":""Meena had ₹40 in her bank account. She bought a school bag for ₹68 using her debit card."",""solutionSteps"":[""Start with Meena’s balance: ₹40."",""She spends ₹68, so subtract 68 from 40."",""Write the integer equation: 40 + (-68) = -28, which is the same as 40 - 68 = -28."",""So her balance is ₹28 below zero.""],""finalAnswer"":""Meena’s new bank balance is -₹28."",""hints"":[""A purchase means the balance goes down."",""If you spend more than you have, the balance becomes negative."",""Subtract 68 from 40.""],""requiresCalculation"":true,""scoringGuidance"":""Award full marks for writing a correct integer equation and giving the final balance as -₹28. Give partial credit if the student gets the correct operation but makes a sign error, or finds 28 without showing that the balance is negative."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learning_objective"":""Students can apply integer operations to real-world contexts such as temperature and debt"",""focus"":""debt""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""323-Starter-5-Q10"",""topicId"":""323"",""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learningObjective"":""Students can apply integer operations to real-world contexts such as temperature and debt"",""levelTag"":""Beginner"",""topicFamily"":""Number Theory"",""grade"":6,""subject"":""Maths"",""questionCount"":1,""testType"":""Starter"",""proficiencyLevel"":""Master"",""questio