326-Starter-8-Q8,mcq,"Sports bottles are packed in cartons of 7. Then 13 extra bottles are placed on a table, making 69 bottles in all. If c is the number of cartons, which equation represents this situation?",Maths,6,Introduction to Algebra,Patterns & Algebra,Students can write equations from real-life situations,Analyzing,hard,5,"3 classroom-ready MCQs on writing equations from real-life situations in Introduction to Algebra, with varied contexts and numbers, and a mix of easy to hard difficulty.","{""options"":[{""text"":""7c + 13 = 69"",""correct"":true},{""text"":""7 + 13c = 69"",""correct"":false},{""text"":""c + 20 = 69"",""correct"":false},{""text"":""69c - 13 = 7"",""correct"":false}],""explanation"":""Each carton has 7 bottles, so cartons give 7c bottles. Adding 13 extra gives a total of 69: 7c + 13 = 69."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Introduction to Algebra"",""subtopic"":""Patterns & Algebra"",""learning_objective"":""Students can write equations from real-life situations"",""focus"":""two-step structure with multiplication and addition""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""326-Starter-8-Q8"",""topicId"":""326"",""topic"":""Introduction to Algebra"",""subtopic"":""Patterns & Algebra"",""learningObjective"":""Students can write equations from real-life situations"",""levelTag"":""Intermediate"",""topicFamily"":""Patterns & Algebra"",""grade"":6,""subject"":""Maths"",""questionCount"":1,""testType"":""Starter"",""proficiencyLevel"":""Pro"",""questionMedium"":""MCQ"",""recentQuestions"":[""Leela saves the same amount each week. After 9 weeks, she has saved ₹72. Which equation shows this situation if s is the amount she saves each week?"",""A fruit seller packs oranges in bags of 6. After adding 11 loose oranges, there are 47 oranges altogether. If b is the number of bags, the equation 6b + 11 = 47 represents this situation."",""A music club charges ₹18 for each badge. If Sohan buys some badges and p