326-Starter-8-Q3,true_false,"True or False: A taxi charges ₹14 for each kilometre travelled. If Meera travels k kilometres and pays ₹112 in total, the equation 14k = 112 represents the situation.",Maths,6,Introduction to Algebra,Patterns & Algebra,Students can write equations from real-life situations,Understanding,easy,1,"Generated 1 true/false item for Grade 6 Maths on writing equations from real-life situations, using new values and a distinct statement pattern.","{""correctAnswer"":true,""explanation"":""This statement is true because the total cost is found by multiplying the cost per kilometre by the number of kilometres. Since the taxi charges ₹14 for each kilometre, 14 × k gives the total cost, so 14k = 112 is the correct equation."",""misconceptionNote"":""Students may confuse repeated equal groups with addition and write 14 + k = 112 instead of using multiplication for '₹14 for each kilometre'."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Introduction to Algebra"",""subtopic"":""Patterns & Algebra"",""learning_objective"":""Students can write equations from real-life situations"",""focus"":""equation from multiplicative cost situation""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""326-Starter-8-Q3"",""topicId"":""326"",""topic"":""Introduction to Algebra"",""subtopic"":""Patterns & Algebra"",""learningObjective"":""Students can write equations from real-life situations"",""levelTag"":""Intermediate"",""topicFamily"":""Patterns & Algebra"",""grade"":6,""subject"":""Maths"",""questionCount"":1,""testType"":""Starter"",""proficiencyLevel"":""Basic"",""questionMedium"":""T/F"",""recentQuestions"":[""Leela saves the same amount each week. After 9 weeks, she has saved ₹72. Which equation shows this situation if s is the amount she saves each week?"",""A fruit seller packs oranges in bags of 6. After adding 11 loose oranges, there are 47 oranges altogether. If b is the number of bags, the equation 6b + 11 = 47 represents this si