326-Starter-8-Q10,word_problem,"If t is the number of strips Maya buys, write an equation to represent this situation.",Maths,6,Introduction to Algebra,Patterns & Algebra,Students can write equations from real-life situations,Applying,medium,2,Generated 1 Grade 6 word problem on writing an equation from a real-life situation within Patterns & Algebra.,"{""scenario"":""At a school fair, game tokens are sold in strips of 7. Maya buys some strips, and then her friend gives her 13 extra tokens. Altogether, Maya has 62 tokens."",""solutionSteps"":[""Each strip has 7 tokens, so the number of tokens from strips is 7t."",""Maya also gets 13 extra tokens."",""The total number of tokens is 62."",""So the equation is 7t + 13 = 62.""],""finalAnswer"":""7t + 13 = 62"",""hints"":[""Look for what is repeated equally each time."",""Add the extra tokens after writing the multiplication part."",""Set the expression equal to the total number of tokens.""],""requiresCalculation"":false,""scoringGuidance"":""Award full marks for writing the equation 7t + 13 = 62. Give partial credit if the student correctly identifies 7t as the repeated amount and 13 as the extra amount but makes a minor equation-order error. Do not award full marks for equations using the wrong operation structure, such as 7 + t = 62."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Introduction to Algebra"",""subtopic"":""Patterns & Algebra"",""learning_objective"":""Students can write equations from real-life situations"",""focus"":null}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""326-Starter-8-Q10"",""topicId"":""326"",""topic"":""Introduction to Algebra"",""subtopic"":""Patterns & Algebra"",""learningObjective"":""Students can write equations from real-life situations"",""levelTag"":""Intermediate"",""topicFamily"":""Patterns & Algebra"",""grade"":6,""subject"":""Maths"",""questionCount"":1,""testType"":""Starter"",""proficiencyLevel"":""Master"",""questionMedium"":""WP"",""recentQues