326-Starter-9-Q10,word_problem,Does n = 4 satisfy the equation 7n + 6 = 34? Show your working and state your answer.,Maths,6,Introduction to Algebra,Patterns & Algebra,Students can identify whether a given value satisfies an equation,Applying,medium,5,"Generated 1 Grade 6 word problem on identifying whether a given value satisfies an equation, aligned to Introduction to Algebra > Patterns & Algebra.","{""scenario"":""A school art club buys sketchbooks. The total cost in dollars is given by the equation 7n + 6 = 34, where n is the number of sketchbooks bought. Liam says that n = 4 makes the equation true."",""solutionSteps"":[""Substitute 4 for n in the equation: 7n + 6 = 34."",""Calculate the left side: 7 × 4 + 6 = 28 + 6."",""Simplify: 28 + 6 = 34."",""Compare both sides: the left side is 34 and the right side is 34, so they are equal."",""Therefore, n = 4 satisfies the equation.""],""finalAnswer"":""Yes, n = 4 satisfies the equation because 7(4) + 6 = 34."",""hints"":[""Replace n with 4 in the equation."",""Work out the left-hand side carefully."",""Check whether your result matches 34.""],""requiresCalculation"":true,""scoringGuidance"":""Award full marks for correctly substituting n = 4, calculating 7 × 4 + 6 = 34, and clearly stating that the value satisfies the equation. Give partial credit if the substitution is correct but there is an arithmetic or conclusion error. No marks for an answer without relevant working unless the correct conclusion is clearly justified."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Introduction to Algebra"",""subtopic"":""Patterns & Algebra"",""learning_objective"":""Students can identify whether a given value satisfies an equation"",""focus"":""Check whether a given value makes an equation true by substitution.""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""326-Starter-9-Q10"",""topicId"":""326"",""topic"":""Introduction to Algebra"",""subtopic"":""Patterns & Algebra"",""learningObjective"":""Stu