322-Starter-10-Q10,word_problem,"If each cargo hub transported the same number of boxes, how many boxes did each hub transport?",Maths,6,Advanced Arithmetic,Number Operations,Students can perform all four operations with numbers up to and beyond 10 million,Applying,hard,5,"Generated 1 Grade 6 Maths word problem on Advanced Arithmetic → Number Operations, aligned to performing operations with numbers up to and beyond 10 million.","{""scenario"":""A shipping company moved 18,936,420 boxes in one year. The boxes were transported equally using 7 cargo hubs."",""solutionSteps"":[""Identify the operation: since the total number of boxes is shared equally among 7 cargo hubs, use division."",""Set up the calculation: 18,936,420 ÷ 7."",""Divide step by step to get 2,705,202 remainder 6."",""So each hub transported 2,705,202 boxes, with 6 boxes left over.""],""finalAnswer"":""Each cargo hub transported 2,705,202 boxes, with 6 boxes remaining."",""hints"":[""Look for the phrase \""shared equally\"" to decide the operation."",""Write the division as 18,936,420 ÷ 7."",""Check your answer by multiplying 2,705,202 by 7.""],""requiresCalculation"":true,""scoringGuidance"":""Award full marks for correctly identifying division, setting up 18,936,420 ÷ 7, and giving the answer 2,705,202 remainder 6 or 2,705,202 with 6 boxes remaining. Award partial marks for a correct method with minor arithmetic errors. Do not award full marks if place value is incorrect or the remainder is omitted when a whole-number exact answer is not possible."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Advanced Arithmetic"",""subtopic"":""Number Operations"",""learning_objective"":""Students can perform all four operations with numbers up to and beyond 10 million"",""focus"":""division with large numbers""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""322-Starter-10-Q10"",""topicId"":""322"",""topic"":""Advanced Arithmetic"",""subtopic"":""Number Operations"",""learningObjectiv