322-Starter-11-Q1,mcq,What is the value of 18 - (4 + 2) × 2²?,Maths,6,Advanced Arithmetic,Number Operations,Students can apply order of operations (BODMAS) including brackets and exponents,Applying,easy,2,"3 classroom-ready Grade 6 MCQs on applying BODMAS with brackets and exponents, with varied difficulty and no reuse of recent standout values.","{""options"":[{""text"":""-6"",""correct"":true},{""text"":""40"",""correct"":false},{""text"":""6"",""correct"":false},{""text"":""20"",""correct"":false}],""explanation"":""Work inside the brackets first: 4 + 2 = 6. Then 2² = 4. Multiply: 6 × 4 = 24. Finally, 18 - 24 = -6."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Advanced Arithmetic"",""subtopic"":""Number Operations"",""learning_objective"":""Students can apply order of operations (BODMAS) including brackets and exponents"",""focus"":""Evaluate an expression using brackets, exponents, multiplication, and subtraction.""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""322-Starter-11-Q1"",""topicId"":""322"",""topic"":""Advanced Arithmetic"",""subtopic"":""Number Operations"",""learningObjective"":""Students can apply order of operations (BODMAS) including brackets and exponents"",""levelTag"":""Expert"",""topicFamily"":""Number Operations"",""grade"":6,""subject"":""Maths"",""questionCount"":1,""testType"":""Starter"",""proficiencyLevel"":""Basic"",""questionMedium"":""MCQ"",""recentQuestions"":[""Which expression has a value of 26?"",""True or False: 15 - (3 + 1) × 2² = -1"",""When evaluated using BODMAS, the expression 10 + 2 × (9 - 4) gives ___"",""Using order of operations, 3² + 4 × (8 - 5) equals ___"",""Match each expression to its correct value. Apply BODMAS carefully: brackets first, then exponents, then multiplication/division, then addition/subtraction."",""Drag each step to the correct stage to show how to evaluate the expression using BODMAS: (9 + 7) ÷ 4 + 3²"",""Evaluate: (9 + 2³) × 3 - 7\nShow each step using BODMAS."",""H