322-Starter-11-Q10,word_problem,How many items are in one complete activity kit altogether? Use BODMAS to calculate.,Maths,6,Advanced Arithmetic,Number Operations,Students can apply order of operations (BODMAS) including brackets and exponents,Applying,medium,5,"Generated 1 Grade 6 word problem on applying BODMAS with brackets and exponents, using a fresh scenario and varied numbers.","{""scenario"":""A science club is packing activity kits for a school fair. Each kit contains 2 trays of samples, and each tray holds (6 + 3) packets. After packing the trays, the club adds 4^2 stickers to each kit for labelling."",""solutionSteps"":[""Write the expression: 2 × (6 + 3) + 4^2"",""Calculate inside the brackets first: 6 + 3 = 9"",""Calculate the exponent: 4^2 = 16"",""Multiply: 2 × 9 = 18"",""Add: 18 + 16 = 34""],""finalAnswer"":""34 items"",""hints"":[""Solve the brackets before multiplying."",""Evaluate the exponent 4^2 before the final addition."",""Follow BODMAS carefully: brackets, orders, multiplication, addition.""],""requiresCalculation"":true,""scoringGuidance"":""Award full marks for forming or using the expression 2 × (6 + 3) + 4^2 and correctly evaluating it to 34. Give partial credit for correctly solving the brackets and/or exponent even if later arithmetic is incorrect. A response showing the correct order of operations should earn marks even with a minor calculation slip."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Advanced Arithmetic"",""subtopic"":""Number Operations"",""learning_objective"":""Students can apply order of operations (BODMAS) including brackets and exponents"",""focus"":null}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""322-Starter-11-Q10"",""topicId"":""322"",""topic"":""Advanced Arithmetic"",""subtopic"":""Number Operations"",""learningObjective"":""Students can apply order of operations (BODMAS) including brackets and exponents"",""levelTag"":""Expert"",""topicFamily"":""Number Operations"",""grade"":6,""subject"":""Maths"",""questionCount"":1,""testType"":""Starter"",""proficiencyLevel"":""Master"",""questionMedium"":""WP"",""recentQuestions"":[""Which expression has a value of 26?"",""True or False: 15 - (3 + 1) × 2² = -1"",""When evaluated using BODMAS, the expression 10 + 2 × (9 - 4) gives ___"",""Using order of operations, 3² + 4 × (8 - 5) equals ___"",""Match each expression to its correct value. Apply BODMAS carefully: brackets first, then exponents, then multiplication/division, then addition/subtraction."",""Drag each step to the correct stage to show how to evaluate the expression using BODMAS: (9 + 7) ÷ 4 + 3²"",""Evaluate: (9 + 2³) × 3 - 7\nShow each step using BODMAS."",""How many sample tubes are in one large box altogether? Use BODMAS to show the order of operations.""],""recentStandoutValues"":[""22"",""14"",""20"",""12"",""10"",""60"",""50"",""39"",""25"",""28"",""31"",""13"",""51"",""44"",""280"",""291""],""avoidNumberReuse"":true,""calibrationExamples"":[{""difficultyBand"":""Basic"",""question"":""What is the correct answer to: 3 + 4 × 2?\nA) 14   B) 11   C) 10   D) 6"",""answer"":""B) 11"",""markingNote"":""Accept B. Students who answer 14 have not applied BODMAS - they added before multiplying. This is a very common error at this level.""},{""difficultyBand"":""Pro"",""question"":""Evaluate: (5² – 3) × 4 + 2³\nShow each step."",""answer"":""(25 – 3) × 4 + 8 = 22 × 4 + 8 = 88 + 8 = 96"",""markingNote"":""Full marks for 96 with correct steps shown. Award partial marks for correct bracket/exponent evaluation even if final arithmetic is wrong. Step-by-step working required.""}],""questionType"":""word_problem""},""batchRequest"":{""topicId"":""322"",""learningObjective"":""Students can apply order of operations (BODMAS) including brackets and exponents"",""testType"":""Starter"",""questionMedium"":""WP"",""queueIds"":[""322-Starter-11-Q10""]},""spec"":{""summary"":""Generated 1 Grade 6 word problem on applying BODMAS with brackets and exponents,