322-Starter-12-Q1,mcq,"Which is the best estimate for 7,384  18?",Maths,6,Advanced Arithmetic,Number Operations,Students can use rounding and approximation to estimate answers,Applying,easy,2,3 classroom-ready Grade 6 MCQs on using rounding and approximation to estimate answers in number operations.,"{""options"":[{""text"":""7,000  20 = 350"",""correct"":false},{""text"":""7,400  20 = 370"",""correct"":true},{""text"":""7,000  10 = 700"",""correct"":false},{""text"":""8,000  20 = 400"",""correct"":false}],""explanation"":""Rounding 7,384 to 7,400 and 18 to 20 gives 7,400  20 = 370, which is a sensible estimate."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Advanced Arithmetic"",""subtopic"":""Number Operations"",""learning_objective"":""Students can use rounding and approximation to estimate answers"",""focus"":""estimating division by sensible rounding""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""322-Starter-12-Q1"",""topicId"":""322"",""topic"":""Advanced Arithmetic"",""subtopic"":""Number Operations"",""learningObjective"":""Students can use rounding and approximation to estimate answers"",""levelTag"":""Expert"",""topicFamily"":""Number Operations"",""grade"":6,""subject"":""Maths"",""questionCount"":1,""testType"":""Starter"",""proficiencyLevel"":""Basic"",""questionMedium"":""MCQ"",""recentQuestions"":[""Which rounding gives the most sensible estimate for 8,596 ÷ 29?"",""To estimate 5,163 ÷ 24, rounding to 5,200 ÷ 25 gives about 208, so saying the quotient is approximately 208 is reasonable."",""Estimate 6,742 × 31 by rounding to the nearest thousand and nearest ten: 6,742 × 31 ≈ ___."",""A delivery company ships 5,186 parcels, each weighing about 44 kg. By rounding 5,186 to the nearest thousand and 44 to the nearest ten, the estimated total weight is ___ kg."",""Match each calculation to its best estimate by rounding the numbers to sensible place values before working out the answer."",""Drag each rounded calculation to the estimate it gives."",""A library buys 612 new books at ₹84 each. Estimate the total cost by rounding each number to make the calculation easy. Show your estimate."",""About how much will the library spend altogether? Estimate the total cost by rounding the numbers to sensible place values, and explain your rounding.""],""recentStandoutValues"":[""40"",""856"",""900"",""478"",""193"",""941"",""087"",""100"",""120"",""700"",""800"",""612"",""84"",""80"",""362"",""54""],""avoidNumberReuse"":true,""calibrationExamples"":[{""difficultyBand"":""Basic"",""question"":""Estimate 4,876 × 21 by rounding each number to the nearest thousand and ten.\nA) 100,000   B) 80,000   C) 90,000   D) 120,000"",""answer"":""A) 100,000"",""markingNote"":""Accept A (5,000 × 20 = 100,000). Accept C if student rounds 4,876 to 5,000 and 21 to 18 - award marks for valid rounding method even with different estimate.""},{""difficultyBand"":""Pro"",""question"":""A school orders 289 chairs at ₹412 each. Without calculating exactly, estimate the total cost and explain how you rounded."",""answer"":""Estimate: 300 × 400 = ₹1,20,000 (approx.)\nExplanation should mention rounding 289 to 300 and 412 to 400."",""markingNote"":""Full marks for a reasonable estimate AND a clear rounding explanation. Accept any rounding strategy as long as it is consistent and explained.""}],""questionType"":""mcq""},""batchRequest"":{""topicId"":""322"",""learningObjective"":""Students can use rounding and approximation to estimate answers"",""testType"":""Starter"",""questionMedium"":""MCQ"",""queueIds"":[""322-Starter-12-Q1"",""322-Starter-12-Q2"",""322-Starter-12-Q8""]},""spec"":{""summary"":""3 classroom-ready Grade 6 MCQs on using rounding and approximation to estimate answers in number operations.""},""deterministicValidation"":{""isValid"":true,""issues"":[]}}"
322-Starter-12-Q2,mcq,"A factory packs 3,271 bottles into boxes. Each box holds 47 bottles. About how many bottles are packed altogether if each group is counted once? Choose the best estimate for 3,271  47.",Maths,6,Advanced Arithmetic,Number Operations,Students can use rounding and approximation to estimate answers,Understanding,medium,3,3 classroom-ready Grade 6 MCQs on using rounding and approximation to estimate answers in number operations.,"{""options"":[{""text"":""3,000  50 = 60"",""correct"":false},{""text"":""3,300  50 = 66"",""correct"":false},{""text"":""3,200  50 = 64"",""correct"":true},{""text"":""3,000  40 = 75"",""correct"":false}],""explanation"":""Rounding 3,271 to 3,200 and 47 to 50 gives 3,200  50 = 64, a close and easy estimate."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Advanced Arithmetic"",""subtopic"":""Number Operations"",""learning_objective"":""Students can use rounding and approximation to estimate answers"",""focus"":""choosing a sensible estimate for division in context""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""322-Starter-12-Q2"",""topicId"":""322"",""topic"":""Advanced Arithmetic"",""subtopic"":""Number Operations"",""learningObjective"":""Students can use rounding and approximation to estimate answers"",""levelTag"":""Expert"",""topicFamily"":""Number Operations"",""grade"":6,""subject"":""Maths"",""questionCount"":1,""testType"":""Starter"",""proficiencyLevel"":""Basic"",""questionMedium"":""MCQ"",""recentQuestions"":[""Which rounding gives the most sensible estimate for 8,596 ÷ 29?"",""To estimate 5,163 ÷ 24, rounding to 5,200 ÷ 25 gives about 208, so saying the quotient is approximately 208 is reasonable."",""Estimate 6,742 × 31 by rounding to the nearest thousand and nearest ten: 6,742 × 31 ≈ ___."",""A delivery company ships 5,186 parcels, each weighing about 44 kg. By rounding 5,186 to the nearest thousand and 44 to the nearest ten, the estimated total weight is ___ kg."",""Mat