322-Starter-13-Q3,true_false,"To calculate 49 × 18 mentally, it is efficient to work out 50 × 18 and then subtract 18, giving 882.",Maths,6,Advanced Arithmetic,Number Operations,Students can apply mental strategies for efficient calculation,Applying,medium,1,"Generated 1 Grade 6 Maths true/false item on applying mental strategies for efficient calculation, avoiding recent number reuse and repeated statement patterns.","{""correctAnswer"":true,""explanation"":""This is true. Since 49 is 1 less than 50, 49 × 18 = (50 × 18) − (1 × 18) = 900 − 18 = 882. Using compensation makes the calculation quicker mentally."",""misconceptionNote"":""Students may forget to subtract one group of 18 after changing 49 to 50, or may think compensation only works for addition."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Advanced Arithmetic"",""subtopic"":""Number Operations"",""learning_objective"":""Students can apply mental strategies for efficient calculation"",""focus"":""compensation in multiplication""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""322-Starter-13-Q3"",""topicId"":""322"",""topic"":""Advanced Arithmetic"",""subtopic"":""Number Operations"",""learningObjective"":""Students can apply mental strategies for efficient calculation"",""levelTag"":""Expert"",""topicFamily"":""Number Operations"",""grade"":6,""subject"":""Maths"",""questionCount"":1,""testType"":""Starter"",""proficiencyLevel"":""Basic"",""questionMedium"":""T/F"",""recentQuestions"":[""A shop sells 18 packs of stickers with 27 stickers in each pack. Which mental method gives the correct total most efficiently?"",""To calculate 297 + 46 mentally, it is efficient to add 300 + 46 and then subtract 3, giving 343."",""Using compensation, 298 + 47 can be found mentally by adding 300 + 47 and then subtracting 2, so the answer is ___."",""A quick mental strategy for 32 × 15 is to work out 32 × 10 and 32 × 5, then add the results, so 32 × 15 = ___."",""Match each calculation to the most efficient mental strategy."",""Match each calculation to the most efficient mental strategy."",""Use a mental strategy to calculate 298 + 46. Show your method."",""How many mystery books are packed altogether? Work it out using an efficient mental strategy.""],""recentStandoutValues"":[""345"",""347"",""460"",""490"",""76"",""39"",""250"",""16"",""84"",""4"",""24"",""67"",""125"",""57"",""75"",""344""],""avoidNumberReuse"":true,""calibrationExamples"":[{""difficultyBand"":""Basic"",""question"":""What is an efficient mental method to calculate 25 × 48?\nA) Multiply normally   B) Double 25 twice and halve 48 twice   C) Multiply 25 × 50 then adjust   D) Split into 20 × 48 + 5 × 48"",""answer"":""C or D (accept both)"",""markingNote"":""Accept C (25 × 50 – 25 × 2 = 1250 – 50 = 1200) or D (960 + 240 = 1200). Both are valid mental strategies. Ask student to explain their method.""},{""difficultyBand"":""Pro"",""question"":""Use a mental strategy to calculate 99 × 13. Show your method."",""answer"":""100 × 13 – 1 × 13 = 1300 – 13 = 1287"",""markingNote"":""Full marks for 1287 with a valid mental strategy shown. Accept alternative valid methods e.g. 99 × 10 + 99 × 3 = 990 + 297 = 1287.""}],""questionType"":""true_false""},""batchRequest"":{""topicId"":""322"",""learningObjective"":""Students can apply mental strategies for efficient calculation"",""testType"":""Starter"",""questionMedium"":""T/F"",""queueIds"":[""322-Starter-13-Q3""]},""spec"":{""summary"":""Generated 1 Grade 6 Maths true/false item on applying mental strategies for efficient calculation, avoiding recent number reuse and repeated statement patterns.""},""deterministicValidation"":{""isValid"":true,""issues"":[]}}"
