322-Starter-13-Q10,word_problem,How many name tags are needed altogether? Work it out using an efficient mental strategy.,Maths,6,Advanced Arithmetic,Number Operations,Students can apply mental strategies for efficient calculation,Applying,hard,1,Generated 1 Grade 6 word problem on applying mental strategies for efficient calculation within Advanced Arithmetic > Number Operations.,"{""scenario"":""A school is preparing welcome packs for a community event. There are 49 tables, and each table needs 26 name tags."",""solutionSteps"":[""Recognize that 49 is close to 50, so use compensation."",""Calculate 50 × 26 = 1300."",""Subtract 1 × 26 = 26 because 49 is 1 less than 50."",""Compute 1300 − 26 = 1274.""],""finalAnswer"":""1274 name tags"",""hints"":[""Think of 49 as 50 minus 1."",""Find 50 groups of 26 first, then adjust.""],""requiresCalculation"":true,""scoringGuidance"":""Award full marks for 1274 with a correct efficient mental strategy, such as 50 × 26 − 26. Give partial credit if the student shows a sensible mental method but makes a small arithmetic error. Minimal credit for the correct operation set up without completion."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Advanced Arithmetic"",""subtopic"":""Number Operations"",""learning_objective"":""Students can apply mental strategies for efficient calculation"",""focus"":""mental strategy using compensation for multiplication""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""322-Starter-13-Q10"",""topicId"":""322"",""topic"":""Advanced Arithmetic"",""subtopic"":""Number Operations"",""learningObjective"":""Students can apply mental strategies for efficient calculation"",""levelTag"":""Expert"",""topicFamily"":""Number Operations"",""grade"":6,""subject"":""Maths"",""questionCount"":1,""testType"":""Starter"",""proficiencyLevel"":""Master"",""questionMedium"":""WP"",""recentQuestions"":[""A shop sells 18 packs of stickers with 27 stickers in each pack. Which mental method gives th