323-Pulse-2-Q5,word_problem,Write the checkpoint elevations in order from least to greatest.,Maths,6,Integers & Operations,Number Theory,Students can compare and order positive and negative integers,Applying,easy,2,Generated 1 Grade 6 word problem on comparing and ordering positive and negative integers within Number Theory.,"{""scenario"":""During a mountain research trip, a team recorded the elevations of several checkpoints relative to sea level. The checkpoints were at -14 m, 7 m, -1 m, 13 m, and 0 m."",""solutionSteps"":[""Identify the negative integers, zero, and positive integers: -14, -1, 0, 7, 13."",""Numbers less than 0 come first, and the more negative a number is, the smaller it is."",""So among the negative integers, -14 is less than -1."",""Then place 0 next, because it is greater than all negative integers and less than all positive integers."",""Finally, order the positive integers from smallest to greatest: 7, 13."",""The full order from least to greatest is -14, -1, 0, 7, 13.""],""finalAnswer"":""-14, -1, 0, 7, 13"",""hints"":[""Negative integers are always less than 0."",""Among negative numbers, the one with the greater distance from 0 is smaller."",""Place 0 between the negative and positive integers.""],""requiresCalculation"":false,""scoringGuidance"":""Award full marks for writing all five integers in the correct order from least to greatest: -14, -1, 0, 7, 13. Give partial credit if the student correctly places all negative integers before 0 and positive integers but makes one ordering mistake within a group. No credit if the ordering does not show understanding of how negative and positive integers compare."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learning_objective"":""Students can compare and order positive and negative integers"",""focus"":""Word problem ordering integers from least to greatest""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""323-Pulse-2-Q5"",""topicId"":""323"",""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learningObjective"":""Students can compare and order positive and negative integers"",""levelTag"":""Beginner"",""topicFamily"":""Number Theory"",""grade"":6,""subject"":""Maths"",""questionCount"":1,""testType"":""Pulse"",""proficiencyLevel"":""Pro"",""questionMedium"":""WP"",""recentQuestions"":[""Order the temperatures from least to greatest."",""Write these integers in order from greatest to least: -6, 4, -2, 0, 9, -11."",""Among the integers -8, 1, 0, and 2, the smallest integer is ___."",""Which list shows these integers in order from least to greatest: -8, 1, -3, 0?"",""Drag each integer into the correct box to show the numbers in order from least to greatest."",""Write these integers in order from least to greatest: -8, 1, -3, 0, 12."",""Write the temperatures in order from least to greatest."",""A scuba diver records these depths relative to sea level: -12 m, 8 m, -3 m, 0 m, and 11 m.\n\nWrite the integers in order from least to greatest. Then explain how you know which integers should come first.""],""recentStandoutValues"":[""3"",""4"",""9"",""-11"",""-8"",""6"",""-3"",""10"",""3"",""4"",""5"",""12"",""-12"",""8"",""-7"",""11""],""avoidNumberReuse"":true,""calibrationExamples"":[{""difficultyBand"":""Basic"",""question"":""Which is smaller: –3 or –7?\nA) –3   B) –7   C) They are equal"",""answer"":""B) –7"",""markingNote"":""Accept B only. A common error is thinking –7 is 'bigger' because 7 > 3 - note this for remediation.""},{""difficultyBand"":""Pro"",""question"":""Arrange in order from least to greatest:\n–5, 3, –1, 0, –8, 4"",""answer"":""–8, –5, –1, 0, 3, 4"",""markingNote"":""All six values in correct order required. Partial credit for correct relative ordering of negatives.""}],""questionType"":""word_problem""},""batchRequest"":{""topicId"":""323"",""learningObjective"":""Students can compare and order positive and negative integers"",""testType"":""Pulse"",""questionMedium"":""WP"",""queueIds"":[""323-Pulse-2-Q5""]},""spec"":{""summary"":""Generated 1 Grade 6 word problem on comparing and ordering positive and negative integers within Number Theory.""},""deterministicValidation"":{""isValid"":true,""issues"":[]}}"
