323-Pulse-3-Q5,word_problem,What is Noah’s score now? Show how you can think about it using integer subtraction or a number line.,Maths,6,Integers & Operations,Number Theory,Students can add and subtract integers using rules and number lines,Applying,easy,2,"Generated 1 beginner Grade 6 word problem on adding/subtracting integers using integer rules/number line language, avoiding recent scenarios and standout values.","{""scenario"":""During a game, Noah starts with 3 points. In the next round, he loses 8 points."",""solutionSteps"":[""Start with 3 points."",""Losing 8 points means subtract 8: 3 - 8."",""On a number line, start at 3 and move 8 spaces to the left."",""You land on -5.""],""finalAnswer"":""Noah’s score is -5 points."",""hints"":[""A loss can be shown with subtraction."",""On a number line, subtracting means move left."",""Count 8 spaces left from 3.""],""requiresCalculation"":true,""scoringGuidance"":""Award full marks for showing the integer operation 3 - 8 and getting -5, or for a correct number line explanation ending at -5. Give partial credit if the student sets up the subtraction correctly but makes a counting error on the number line, or if they give -5 without explanation when working is requested."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learning_objective"":""Students can add and subtract integers using rules and number lines"",""focus"":null}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""323-Pulse-3-Q5"",""topicId"":""323"",""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learningObjective"":""Students can add and subtract integers using rules and number lines"",""levelTag"":""Beginner"",""topicFamily"":""Number Theory"",""grade"":6,""subject"":""Maths"",""questionCount"":1,""testType"":""Pulse"",""proficiencyLevel"":""Pro"",""questionMedium"":""WP"",""recentQuestions"":[""What is the temperature in the afternoon?"",""Start at -8