323-Pulse-4-Q5,word_problem,What is the player's final score change? Show the steps and state whether the answer is positive or negative.,Maths,6,Integers & Operations,Number Theory,Students can multiply and divide integers and determine the sign of the result,Applying,medium,2,Generated 1 Grade 6 Maths word problem on multiplying and dividing integers and determining the sign of the result.,"{""scenario"":""A game player starts with a score change of -27 points after hitting a penalty zone. The game divides that penalty equally across 3 rounds, and then the result is multiplied by -4 because of a bonus reversal card."",""solutionSteps"":[""Start with the integer expression: (-27) ÷ 3 × (-4)."",""Divide first: (-27) ÷ 3 = -9."",""Then multiply: -9 × (-4) = 36."",""A negative divided by a positive is negative, and a negative multiplied by a negative is positive."",""So the final score change is 36, which is positive.""],""finalAnswer"":""36, positive"",""hints"":[""Divide before multiplying, working from left to right."",""Remember: negative ÷ positive = negative."",""Remember: negative × negative = positive.""],""requiresCalculation"":true,""scoringGuidance"":""Award full marks for a correct calculation of 36 and for stating that the result is positive. Give partial credit if the student correctly computes (-27) ÷ 3 = -9 but makes an error in the final multiplication or sign. Also give partial credit if the numerical value 36 is correct but the sign description is missing."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learning_objective"":""Students can multiply and divide integers and determine the sign of the result"",""focus"":null}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""323-Pulse-4-Q5"",""topicId"":""323"",""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learningObjective"":""Students can multiply and divide integers and determine the sign of the r