323-Pulse-5-Q4,short_answer,Mina has ₹240 in her bank account. She pays a bill of ₹315 using her debit card. Write an integer equation to represent the transaction and find her new account balance.,Maths,6,Integers & Operations,Number Theory,Students can apply integer operations to real-world contexts such as temperature and debt,Applying,medium,2,"Generated 1 Grade 6 short-answer item on applying integer operations in a real-world debt context, aligned to the specified learning objective and avoiding recent wording and number reuse.","{""modelAnswer"":""240 - 315 = -75, so her new account balance is ₹-75 (₹75 overdrawn)."",""scoringGuidance"":""Full marks for a correct integer equation and the correct final balance of -75. Accept equivalent equations such as 240 + (-315) = -75. Partial credit if the equation shows correct operation but the final sign or value is incorrect."",""expectedResponseLength"":""two_to_three_sentences"",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learning_objective"":""Students can apply integer operations to real-world contexts such as temperature and debt"",""focus"":""debt context with integer subtraction""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""323-Pulse-5-Q4"",""topicId"":""323"",""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learningObjective"":""Students can apply integer operations to real-world contexts such as temperature and debt"",""levelTag"":""Beginner"",""topicFamily"":""Number Theory"",""grade"":6,""subject"":""Maths"",""questionCount"":1,""testType"":""Pulse"",""proficiencyLevel"":""Pro"",""questionMedium"":""SA"",""recentQuestions"":[""What is the temperature in the afternoon? Write an integer equation and find the answer."",""On Monday morning, the temperature was 6°C. That night, it dropped by 14°C. What was the temperature at night? Show the integer equation you used."",""A submarine was at 9 m below se