323-Pulse-5-Q5,word_problem,"Write an integer equation to represent Meera’s new account balance, and find the balance after the payment.",Maths,6,Integers & Operations,Number Theory,Students can apply integer operations to real-world contexts such as temperature and debt,Applying,easy,2,"Generated 1 Grade 6 word problem on applying integer operations in a real-world context of debt, aligned to the provided learning objective and avoiding recent scenario/value repetition.","{""scenario"":""Meera has ₹240 in her bank account. She pays a bill of ₹315 using her debit card."",""solutionSteps"":[""Start with the account balance: +240."",""A payment of ₹315 is represented by -315."",""Write the integer equation: 240 + (-315) = 240 - 315."",""Subtract 315 from 240 to get -75."",""So Meera’s new account balance is -₹75, which means she is overdrawn by ₹75.""],""finalAnswer"":""240 + (-315) = -75, so Meera’s new balance is -₹75."",""hints"":[""A payment decreases the balance, so use a negative integer."",""Start with the initial balance, then add the negative amount spent."",""If the result is negative, the account is overdrawn.""],""requiresCalculation"":true,""scoringGuidance"":""Award full marks for: (1) writing a correct integer equation such as 240 + (-315) = -75 or 240 - 315 = -75, and (2) stating the final balance as -₹75 or ₹75 overdrawn. Give partial credit if the equation is correct but the final sign is wrong, or if the student gets -75 without showing an equation."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learning_objective"":""Students can apply integer operations to real-world contexts such as temperature and debt"",""focus"":""debt""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""323-Pulse-5-Q5"",""topicId"":""323"",""topic"":""Integers & Operations"",""subtopic"":""Number Theory"",""learningObjective"":""Students can apply integer operations to real-world contexts such