326-Pulse-6-Q5,word_problem,"Look at the expression 10p + 16 - 8q.
(a) Identify the variables.
(b) Identify the constant.
(c) What is the coefficient of p?
(d) What is the coefficient of q?",Maths,6,Introduction to Algebra,Patterns & Algebra,"Students can identify variables, constants, and coefficients in algebraic expressions",Understanding,medium,2,"Generated 1 Grade 6 word problem on identifying variables, constants, and coefficients in algebraic expressions, using a fresh scenario and avoiding recent standout values.","{""scenario"":""A school fair sells snack boxes and juice cups. The total money collected is represented by the expression 10p + 16 - 8q, where p is the number of snack boxes sold and q is the number of discount coupons used."",""solutionSteps"":[""The letters in an algebraic expression are called variables."",""In 10p + 16 - 8q, the letters are p and q, so these are the variables."",""The number without a variable is the constant."",""In this expression, 16 has no letter, so the constant is 16."",""The coefficient is the number multiplying a variable."",""For p, the term is 10p, so the coefficient of p is 10."",""For q, the term is -8q, so the coefficient of q is -8.""],""finalAnswer"":""(a) Variables: p and q\n(b) Constant: 16\n(c) Coefficient of p: 10\n(d) Coefficient of q: -8"",""hints"":[""Look for letters to find the variables."",""The constant is the number with no letter attached."",""The coefficient is the number in front of the variable.""],""requiresCalculation"":false,""scoringGuidance"":""Award 1 mark for identifying both variables (p and q), 1 mark for the constant (16), 1 mark for the coefficient of p (10), and 1 mark for the coefficient of q (-8). Accept 8 for the coefficient of q only if sign convention is being treated leniently, but note that -8 is the complete correct answer."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Introduction to Algebra"",""subtopic"":""Patterns & Algebra"",""learning_objective"":""Students can identify variables, constants, and coefficients in algebraic expressions"",""focus"":null}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId