k boxes and spends ₹96 altogether. Which equation represents this situation if the number of snack boxes is s?"",""Drag each part to build the equation that matches this situation: A taxi charges a fixed booking fee of ₹12 and ₹7 for each kilometre traveled. The total fare is ₹68. Match each expression to its place in the equation."",""A fruit seller packs oranges in bags with 7 oranges in each bag. After adding 11 extra oranges, there are 60 oranges altogether. Write an equation to show this situation."",""Write an equation to represent this situation, and find how many tickets Arjun bought."",""A fruit seller packs oranges into bags with 7 oranges in each bag. Then 11 extra oranges are placed outside the bags. There are 81 oranges in all. Write an equation to represent this situation, and find how many bags were packed.""],""recentStandoutValues"":[""48"",""35"",""245"",""210"",""280"",""6"",""12"",""96"",""7"",""68"",""11"",""60"",""8"",""81"",""70"",""10""],""avoidNumberReuse"":true,""calibrationExamples"":[{""difficultyBand"":""Basic"",""question"":""Tickets to a show cost ₹60 each. Ravi buys some tickets and pays ₹300 total. Which equation fits?\nA) 60 + t = 300   B) 60t = 300   C) t ÷ 60 = 300   D) t – 60 = 300"",""answer"":""B) 60t = 300"",""markingNote"":""Accept B. If student selects A, they are confusing multiplication with addition structure - use to reteach.""},{""difficultyBand"":""Pro"",""question"":""A shopkeeper has some boxes. After receiving 15 more, he has 48 boxes in total. Write an equation and find the number of boxes he started with."",""answer"":""b + 15 = 48 → b = 33"",""markingNote"":""Full marks for correct equation AND solution. Award partial marks for correct equation with arithmetic error in solving.""}],""questionType"":""mcq""},""batchRequest"":{""topicId"":""326"",""learningObjective"":""Students can write equations from real-life situations"",""testType"":""Pulse"",""questionMedium"":""MCQ"",""queueIds"":[""326-Pulse-8-Q2""]},""spe