326-Pulse-9-Q1,fitb,"For the equation 6m - 5 = 43, the value m = 8 ___ the equation.",Maths,6,Introduction to Algebra,Patterns & Algebra,Students can identify whether a given value satisfies an equation,Understanding,easy,2,A 1-item Grade 6 Maths FITB question bank on identifying whether a given value satisfies an equation.,"{""answer"":""satisfies"",""distractors"":[""does not satisfy"",""solves for 10"",""changes""],""hint"":""Substitute 8 for m and check whether both sides are equal."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Introduction to Algebra"",""subtopic"":""Patterns & Algebra"",""learning_objective"":""Students can identify whether a given value satisfies an equation"",""focus"":""substitute a value into a one-step linear equation to check equality""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""326-Pulse-9-Q1"",""topicId"":""326"",""topic"":""Introduction to Algebra"",""subtopic"":""Patterns & Algebra"",""learningObjective"":""Students can identify whether a given value satisfies an equation"",""levelTag"":""Intermediate"",""topicFamily"":""Patterns & Algebra"",""grade"":6,""subject"":""Maths"",""questionCount"":1,""testType"":""Pulse"",""proficiencyLevel"":""Basic"",""questionMedium"":""FIB"",""recentQuestions"":[""Does n = 6 satisfy the equation 4n + 3 = 27? Show your working."",""Check whether n = 5 satisfies the equation 4n + 3 = 22. Show your working and write a conclusion."",""For the equation 2p + 8 = 18, the value p = 5 ___ the equation."",""A box has value 8. Does this value satisfy the equation 2p + 9 = 25?"",""Drag each value to the correct box to show whether it satisfies the equation 3p + 8 = 26."",""Check whether p = 8 satisfies the equation 5p - 9 = 31. Show your working and write a conclusion."",""Does p = 11 satisfy the equation p + 8 = 19? Show your working and write a conclusion."",""Substitute the value into the equation to check it.\n\nDoes p = 8 satisfy the equation 3p + 2 = 26?\nShow your workin