326-Pulse-9-Q5,word_problem,Mia thinks that k = 7 makes the equation true. Does k = 7 satisfy the equation 6k + 5 = 47? Show your working and write a conclusion.,Maths,6,Introduction to Algebra,Patterns & Algebra,Students can identify whether a given value satisfies an equation,Applying,medium,3,"Generated 1 Grade 6 word problem on identifying whether a given value satisfies an equation, using a fresh scenario and avoiding recent repeated values and setups.","{""scenario"":""Mia is packing art kits for a school club. The total number of items in one kit is given by the equation 6k + 5 = 47, where k is the number of paintbrushes packs added."",""solutionSteps"":[""Substitute 7 for k in the equation: 6k + 5 = 47."",""Calculate the left side: 6 × 7 + 5 = 42 + 5 = 47."",""Compare both sides: 47 = 47."",""Since both sides are equal, k = 7 satisfies the equation.""],""finalAnswer"":""Yes, k = 7 satisfies the equation because 6 × 7 + 5 = 47."",""hints"":[""Replace k with 7 in the equation."",""Work out the left-hand side carefully."",""Check whether your result matches 47.""],""requiresCalculation"":true,""scoringGuidance"":""Award full marks for: correct substitution of k = 7, accurate calculation of 6 × 7 + 5 = 47, and a clear conclusion that the value satisfies the equation. Give partial credit if the student substitutes correctly but makes an arithmetic error, or if the working is correct but the conclusion is missing."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Introduction to Algebra"",""subtopic"":""Patterns & Algebra"",""learning_objective"":""Students can identify whether a given value satisfies an equation"",""focus"":""value substitution to test an equation""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""326-Pulse-9-Q5"",""topicId"":""326"",""topic"":""Introduction to Algebra"",""subtopic"":""Patterns & Algebra"",""learningObjective"":""Students can identify whether a given value satisfies an equation"",""levelTag"":""Intermedi