322-Pulse-11-Q1,fitb,"After applying BODMAS, the value of (4 + 3²) × 3 - 5 is ___.",Maths,6,Advanced Arithmetic,Number Operations,Students can apply order of operations (BODMAS) including brackets and exponents,Applying,medium,1,"Generated 1 Grade 6 Maths fill-in-the-blank item on applying BODMAS with brackets and exponents, using varied values and avoiding recent stem patterns and standout numbers.","{""answer"":""34"",""distractors"":[""22"",""46"",""52""],""hint"":""Work out the exponent first, then the brackets, then multiply, and finally subtract."",""metadata"":{""subject"":""Maths"",""grade"":6,""topic"":""Advanced Arithmetic"",""subtopic"":""Number Operations"",""learning_objective"":""Students can apply order of operations (BODMAS) including brackets and exponents"",""focus"":""Evaluate an expression with brackets, an exponent, multiplication, and subtraction using BODMAS""}}","{""source"":""grade6-workbook"",""request"":{""queueId"":""322-Pulse-11-Q1"",""topicId"":""322"",""topic"":""Advanced Arithmetic"",""subtopic"":""Number Operations"",""learningObjective"":""Students can apply order of operations (BODMAS) including brackets and exponents"",""levelTag"":""Expert"",""topicFamily"":""Number Operations"",""grade"":6,""subject"":""Maths"",""questionCount"":1,""testType"":""Pulse"",""proficiencyLevel"":""Basic"",""questionMedium"":""FIB"",""recentQuestions"":[""What total score does Tara get? Show the steps using the correct order of operations."",""Evaluate the expression below using BODMAS. Show each step clearly.\n\n(7 + 2^3) × 5 - 6"",""After applying BODMAS, the value of 3 + (5 × 2²) - 4 is ___."",""What is the value of the expression 3 + (9 - 4) × 2³?"",""Drag each expression to its correct value after evaluating using BODMAS."",""Evaluate the expression using BODMAS. Show each step clearly.\n\n(9 + 2²) × 6 - 11"",""What is Leo’s total score? Evaluate the expression (3 + 2²) × 2 + 14 using BODMAS. Show each step."",""Simplify the expression below usin